WEBVTT

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.435
Do you know about Season Fairies?

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:09.743
They're tiny fairies that make
rainfall, snowfall, wind, and clouds...

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:13.046
Waffo! That's me!
I'm Snow Fairy Sugar!

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.914
I'm Sun Fairy Salt!

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.018
My name is Wind Fairy Pepper.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.282
You're still apprentices, remember?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.618
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.863
Kuchibiru ni

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:35.096
Namida no rouge

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.991
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:05.022
Ai nante, Shiritaku naiwa

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:12.338
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.442
Kuchibiru ni

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:20.436
Namida no rouge

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.920
Mokuyo ni

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.889
Bara o kai

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:33.791
Tegami o soete

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:41.360
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.129
Yume de au

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.230
Anata wa yasashii

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.089
You guys hold that side down.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.455
-Okay.
-Is this good?
-Thanks.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.660
When's this gonna start?

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.287
Any moment now!

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.032
Okay, this should do it.
Let's try it again!

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.465
Yeah!

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.208
See? It's about to start,
Salt! LOOK!

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.250
Ignition.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.629
Good!

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.710
See? See? That's a "Twinkle"!
This time it's the real thing!

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.712
Good, just a little more.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.907
This is a "Twinkle"?

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.380
-Phil, how is it?
-Just a little more!

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.886
-Phil, is it done yet?
-Not yet!

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.514
Good. Keep it coming! Keep it coming!

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.857
Good!

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.326
Okay...

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.566
-Stop! Stop! Stop!
-Hey, stop! Stop!

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.362
Huh?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.111
That was scary.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.681
That can't be a "Twinkle".

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:38.811
I've never heard of
a "Twinkle" that explodes.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.482
Salt!

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.229
What happened to you guys?

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.637
Nothing much.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.573
Nothing much!
But, you're all scratched up!

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:04.244
You're overreacting.
These scratches don't hurt a bit.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:08.514
You were probably doing another
nutty experiment, and it failed again.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:13.508
Nutty? We were just doing
a scientific experiment. Right?

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.990
That's why I called it nutty.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.685
Saga.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.395
Sugar! I told you not to come to school.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.761
Hey! Th-That's him!

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:28.968
Thanks to him, I had a
horrible time yesterday.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.070
Hey! What'd you do that for!

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.405
That jerk!

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.973
Did something happen?

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:37.238
Well, something I thought
was a "Twinkle" went...

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.813
...BOOM! And then Salt went...

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.516
...ARGH! And that's what happened.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.517
What?

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.111
So, what kind of an
experiment was it?

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:50.056
Do you want to know?
Do you really want to know?

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:53.492
You've twisted my arm.
Okay, I'll tell you.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:02.601
Listen and be amazed. Yesterday,
I was attempting to make an aurora.

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:04.901
An aurora?

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:09.434
By aurora, do you mean the one that
appears at the North or South Pole?

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.312
That's right. That kind
of aurora!

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.379
Alley-oop!

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:18.151
It won't be as big as the real thing,
but I can make one artificially.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:21.554
Just one more push, and
I would have succeeded, too.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.423
Right? It shone a bit, didn't it?

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:26.426
-It did?
-Did it?

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.429
Yeah! Yeah! It shone!
It went Twinkle-twinkle!

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.897
Did Sugar think?

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:35.459
Yes. Sugar mistook that
light for a "Twinkle".

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.068
I thought so.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:42.269
Just a second! Was this guy
trying to make an aurora?

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:46.813
Are you kidding? Auroras are
mysterious natural phenomena...

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:50.783
...that you can only see in cold places.
Do you seriously think...

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:55.021
...you can make something like that?
There's no way you can!

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.785
Ah, but I can.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.991
Ta-dah!

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:05.031
Listen, everyone!
The problem is air pressure.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:08.034
Yesterday's experiment failed
because I pumped air...

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:11.437
...into something that should
have had its air thinned.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.769
That's why, this time
I'll fix the pump...

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:18.478
I get it! I should redesign
the pump part! Yeah!

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:20.673
This kid is hopeless.
Completely hopeless.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.516
Sorry, Phil, but...

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:28.888
I have a feeling that Greta's
finally right this time. Right, Saga?

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:30.014
Yeah...

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:35.584
Yeah, I'll do that. If I do that, I should
be able to make an aurora this time!

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:39.529
An aurora? Is this guy serious?

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.460
Okay. This time I'll succeed for sure!

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:48.374
So you see, the more the air
is heated, the more it rises.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:50.343
Now, let's try the experiment.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.810
Okay!

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:56.382
Saga goes first.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:57.849
Okay, here goes.

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:01.921
It's flying! It's flying!

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.523
It's Puffy-fluffy!

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:09.662
I'm saying an aurora is difficult magic
even for a full-fledged Sun Fairy.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.165
There's no way he can do it.

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:16.102
It might have been small yesterday,
but he made a pretty light.

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.037
That's true.

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:20.440
That thing wasn't an aurora!

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:24.433
In the first place, it's our job to
control the weather as Season Fairies.

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:28.447
That's fine, but don't get in
the way of the experiment, okay?

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:32.418
All right.

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:35.455
C-C'mon. Don't do it.

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.855
Yeah. I have a bad feeling about it.

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.993
Hey, you! Stop experimenting!

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:45.287
So, are your experiments
going smoothly? Okay then...

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.564
Is everyone okay?

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:57.008
Wh-What?

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:00.739
See? I told you it wouldn't work!

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:05.585
-Salt!
-Are you all right?

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.052
Ow, ow, ow...

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:10.389
You boys!

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:16.496
Stand there and think about what you did!

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.464
Yes, Teacher.

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:21.558
That's funny... I was so close.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.637
What's with this guy? Sheesh.

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:38.417
Why can't he understand that
he can't possibly make an aurora?

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:40.920
He should know it's hopeless.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.321
There's no reason for you to
be so upset about it, is there?

00:08:44.891 --> 00:08:48.427
I don't think there's anything
wrong with Phil experimenting.

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:51.624
Sugar, what do you want
to be when you grow up?

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:55.422
Naturally, I want to be a proud
Snow Fairy like my mommy.

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:58.004
I'm going to make
lots of pretty snowfall.

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.338
What about you, Pepper?

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:02.408
Naturally, a proud Wind Fairy.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:05.711
And my dream is to
become a proud Sun Fairy.

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:11.984
But it's extremely difficult to
become a full-fledged Season Fairy.

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:14.384
It's not something
a human can do easily.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:20.019
It's our job to control the
weather as Season Fairies!

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:45.318
Hey, Saga. Saga! Let's have a waffo
on the way home. Waffo! Waffo!

00:09:45.318 --> 00:09:49.152
I keep telling you, they're
not waffos: They're waffles.

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:54.126
Hi, Saga!

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:56.959
Are you alone, Phil?
Where are Alan and Jan?

00:09:57.096 --> 00:10:00.433
Alan is at home, because his uncle is visiting,
or something.

00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:03.002
Jan said his aunt was visiting,
or something.

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:05.605
They both said they probably
can't help out for a while.

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:09.041
Oh, well. I can do the
experiment without them.

00:10:10.576 --> 00:10:11.907
Are you okay, Phil?

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:15.047
I guess I'll have to help.

00:10:15.047 --> 00:10:17.450
Oh, th-thanks!

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.577
J-Just for a little while, okay?

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:31.163
Say, Saga? If I really do make an aurora,
don't you think that would be amazing?

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:34.066
Yeah. Everyone would be shocked.

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:36.432
You think? That's for sure!

00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:41.505
Are you experimenting because you want
to shock everyone? Even if you get hurt?

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:47.446
Actually, my dream is to become
a famous scientist some day!

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:51.283
A scientist so amazing,
he makes everybody freak.

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:55.151
This experiment is like practice.

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:57.990
What's a scientist?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:00.356
I don't know. I wonder...

00:11:00.559 --> 00:11:03.596
You know! Scientists are cool, right?

00:11:03.596 --> 00:11:04.688
I gotcha.

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:09.769
Scientists can do all kinds of things!
Stuff that makes people's jaws drop.

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:11.003
Are you listening, Saga?

00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:12.868
I'm listening.

00:11:23.349 --> 00:11:25.078
That's what he said.

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:28.754
I'm saying that's the job of a Sun Fairy.

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:33.350
Why is this scientist guy
trying to make an aurora?

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:35.858
Only a Sun Fairy can make an aurora!

00:11:35.995 --> 00:11:37.963
Yes, that's true, but...

00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:41.528
Salt!

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:45.603
Salt...

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:58.711
I've never tried aurora magic before...

00:12:10.896 --> 00:12:13.364
It's not supposed to be like this!
One more time!

00:12:21.974 --> 00:12:23.441
It's no good.

00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:28.413
Again!

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:44.396
It still needs work.

00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:48.333
Oops, now I've done it.

00:12:49.101 --> 00:12:52.628
L-I'm sorry! I'll move this out of your way!

00:12:54.173 --> 00:12:56.141
What's he doing?

00:12:57.576 --> 00:12:59.043
That guy...

00:13:06.719 --> 00:13:10.389
I see. I guess vinyl is
too weak to hold it.

00:13:10.389 --> 00:13:12.357
It's a problem of strength.

00:13:14.293 --> 00:13:17.592
He doesn't learn. It's hopeless
no matter how he tries.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:23.597
Okay, how about transparent plastic?
No, I should just use glass.

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:26.972
I keep telling you, it's hopeless.

00:13:26.972 --> 00:13:31.341
Oh, well. I don't have time
to hang around this loser.

00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:35.345
Okay, let's do this!
Where's my pencil?

00:13:35.414 --> 00:13:37.382
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:41.854
Where'd it go?

00:13:41.854 --> 00:13:44.084
That's strange.

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:47.058
Sheesh, you're hopeless.

00:13:49.161 --> 00:13:50.628
Oh, well!

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:55.532
So he's going to make an aurora.

00:13:56.869 --> 00:14:00.072
I didn't know there were humans
who thought about that sort of thing.

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:02.040
That's interesting.

00:14:03.509 --> 00:14:06.478
But you know, Salt is furious.

00:14:06.478 --> 00:14:12.418
He said that making auroras is
Sun Fairy work and went somewhere.

00:14:12.418 --> 00:14:17.489
That makes sense. At any rate,
maybe I'll go to see this Phil fellow.

00:14:17.489 --> 00:14:18.979
Where is he?

00:14:19.892 --> 00:14:23.658
The glass jar has to be bigger, or it won't work.

00:14:24.797 --> 00:14:28.528
Do I have a glass jar just the right size here?

00:14:29.468 --> 00:14:30.492
I don't.

00:14:30.636 --> 00:14:32.438
Then give up.

00:14:32.438 --> 00:14:33.735
Oh!

00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:35.468
Here we go!

00:14:38.777 --> 00:14:40.404
This'll do.

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:42.514
Wh-Why am I?

00:14:42.948 --> 00:14:44.415
I saw that!

00:14:46.485 --> 00:14:49.054
Salt, you've been helping out Phil.

00:14:49.054 --> 00:14:53.392
That must be hard.
Shall we help out, as well?

00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:55.027
I agree!

00:14:55.027 --> 00:14:59.465
D-Don't get the wrong idea.
I just couldn't stand to watch.

00:14:59.465 --> 00:15:01.558
Salt, hurry! Hurry!

00:15:02.601 --> 00:15:03.932
Darn.

00:15:14.513 --> 00:15:15.447
Phil!

00:15:15.447 --> 00:15:16.715
Hi, Saga.

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:17.807
Waffo!

00:15:18.217 --> 00:15:20.344
Wh-What are you doing?

00:15:20.486 --> 00:15:23.355
You know! I'm collecting materials.

00:15:23.355 --> 00:15:25.958
We're all helping out Phil.

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:28.153
I'm just watching, understand?

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:30.360
Why are you doing that?

00:15:30.496 --> 00:15:32.431
For my experiment, of course.

00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:35.100
I just have a little more
to go before it's complete.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:38.729
The three of us are collecting
all kinds of materials for him.

00:15:43.342 --> 00:15:44.673
This is cute!

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.835
This is wonderful, too!

00:15:47.012 --> 00:15:48.809
This is fun-looking, too!

00:15:49.515 --> 00:15:50.982
We did it!

00:15:54.053 --> 00:15:55.680
Okay, let's go!

00:15:55.821 --> 00:15:56.879
Yeah!

00:15:57.022 --> 00:16:00.458
Huh? Was it shaped
like this before? Oh, well!

00:16:00.592 --> 00:16:02.958
Okay, ignition!

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.668
Hip, hip, hooray! Hip, hip, hooray!

00:16:10.502 --> 00:16:12.404
-Saga?
-What's wrong?

00:16:12.404 --> 00:16:14.463
All right. I'll help out, too!

00:16:14.606 --> 00:16:16.005
Huh? Are you sure?

00:16:16.141 --> 00:16:19.338
Really? All right!
We're all helping together!

00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:44.930
It's finally going to be tomorrow.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:48.957
We're going to unveil it to
everyone. I hope it succeeds.

00:17:49.568 --> 00:17:51.437
Do you think it will succeed?

00:17:51.437 --> 00:17:54.531
It's okay! Phil is a scientist! Right?

00:17:58.544 --> 00:18:00.535
I sure hope so.

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:07.519
Ahem!

00:18:07.519 --> 00:18:11.512
Thank you for coming here so
early in the morning, everyone.

00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:15.094
You are very fortunate,
for you are about to witness...

00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:18.120
...the greatest discovery
of the millennium!

00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:23.969
Did he complete that all by himself?

00:18:23.969 --> 00:18:26.699
It looks like Saga helped him.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:30.375
When did Saga take an interest?

00:18:30.375 --> 00:18:33.833
Maybe those two actually
have a lot in common.

00:18:35.781 --> 00:18:39.615
But still, I didn't think that
you'd come here, too, Greta.

00:18:40.219 --> 00:18:43.518
Who's the one who came
and woke me up?

00:18:45.557 --> 00:18:50.496
Well, shall we begin?
Assistant Saga, are you ready?

00:18:50.496 --> 00:18:51.897
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:51.897 --> 00:18:55.924
Very well. Let us observe
my greatest invention...

00:18:56.068 --> 00:18:58.036
...the Aurora Machine No. 2!!

00:19:04.276 --> 00:19:06.005
I'm excited, aren't you?

00:19:06.145 --> 00:19:08.680
Do you think it will really succeed?

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.980
Phil's idea appears to be perfect, but...

00:19:13.886 --> 00:19:16.446
Okay, Miss Saga. Ignition!

00:19:42.648 --> 00:19:44.115
Phil!

00:19:47.653 --> 00:19:48.551
Salt!

00:19:49.154 --> 00:19:50.280
Not yet!

00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:54.557
Don't disappear!
You can't disappear!

00:19:54.693 --> 00:19:56.524
Keep trying!
Pull yourself together!

00:19:56.662 --> 00:19:59.028
Hey! Shine like you're supposed to!

00:19:59.164 --> 00:20:01.029
Aw, it'll go out!

00:20:02.634 --> 00:20:05.535
Shine, darn you!

00:20:37.336 --> 00:20:39.133
It's pretty!

00:20:47.212 --> 00:20:49.009
It's so pretty...

00:20:49.948 --> 00:20:51.783
Are you all right?

00:20:51.783 --> 00:20:56.516
Hey, Salt? When did you learn
to use that kind of magic?

00:20:57.055 --> 00:20:58.890
It's not my power.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:20:59.754
Huh?

00:21:00.392 --> 00:21:04.096
I could never make that kind
of light with my magic alone.

00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:06.428
That's Phil's invention!

00:21:17.542 --> 00:21:19.442
Phil, that's amazing!

00:21:19.911 --> 00:21:21.879
Thank you, everyone!

00:21:24.082 --> 00:21:25.379
Saga!

00:21:25.517 --> 00:21:29.544
Saga, isn't it amazing?
Scientists can make seasons, too!

00:21:29.688 --> 00:21:31.417
Yeah, it's like a dream.

00:21:31.556 --> 00:21:35.394
Say, Phil will become
a scientist for sure!

00:21:35.394 --> 00:21:38.664
That's true. You might
be right about that.

00:21:38.664 --> 00:21:41.033
You could be a scientist, too.

00:21:41.033 --> 00:21:44.036
I won't be a scientist.

00:21:44.036 --> 00:21:49.372
You won't? Then what do you want
to be? What's your dream, Saga?

00:21:49.508 --> 00:21:51.533
Well... My dream is...

00:21:51.677 --> 00:21:53.338
Oh! It's disappearing!

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:01.781
Okay! I got it fixed! Let's go!

00:22:20.839 --> 00:22:24.832
Tsuki no negai

00:22:25.344 --> 00:22:28.880
Mizu ni tokete

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:34.250
Shiroi namiki-michi mitsuketa

00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:38.152
Hoshi-kuzu no uta

00:22:39.057 --> 00:22:47.432
Nana-iro no hashi o wataru kaze

00:22:47.432 --> 00:22:52.699
Shitte ita yo ne

00:22:52.838 --> 00:22:57.502
Kimochi tsunagu ureshisa

00:22:57.642 --> 00:22:59.872
Sugar Snow

00:23:00.011 --> 00:23:07.611
Kona-yuki mau machi ni yagate

00:23:07.753 --> 00:23:13.020
Kirei na hana saku kisetsu ni

00:23:13.158 --> 00:23:17.720
Anata o omou

00:23:19.598 --> 00:23:24.035
Kokoro o tokasu

00:23:24.169 --> 00:23:28.299
ai wa, yume wa

00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:35.312
sono mune ni aruno

00:23:39.851 --> 00:23:40.619
Preview of the Next Episode

00:23:40.619 --> 00:23:43.555
Preview of the Next Episode
Let's see... For starters,
I want a "pretty snow-making machine,"

00:23:43.555 --> 00:23:46.057
and a "waffo-making machine," and...

00:23:46.057 --> 00:23:48.493
I know! I also want
a "Twinkle Detector"!

00:23:48.493 --> 00:23:51.430
Just a minute, Sugar. Are you thinking
of getting Phil to make all those?

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:55.567
Yeah! I hope Phil becomes
a full-fledged scientist quick.

00:23:55.567 --> 00:23:59.037
Actually, you should
become full-fledged first!

00:23:59.037 --> 00:24:02.574
"A Little Snow Fairy Sugar"
The next episode is
"The Bear Pianist"

00:24:02.574 --> 00:24:05.544
What an odd person Mr. Vincent is.

00:24:05.544 --> 00:24:07.011
Yeah.
